148:| S142 | git-log documentation — https://git-scm.com/docs/git-log | docs | A | the `--diff-merges` format set, in particular `first-parent`, which is the arm a freeze gate needs to see a merge's own resolution edit | Page fetched 2026-10-28 (HTTP 200, 375,834 bytes, sha256 `0a73e33b235368af3021b6dc7dbca11ca4b513157ac651acf548d94e1a5c4a1a`); anchor `--diff-merges=<format>`, value `first-parent` | With `--diff-merges=first-parent` a merge's diff is taken against its first parent only, the same shape `--patch` gives a non-merge commit, so a gate can read a resolution edit. | mined | 2026-10-28 | on-release | corpus/lessons/round-46.md |
